Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.15,0:00:13.76,Low,,0,0,0,,A printed box with a hinged lid. Left: the original part. Right: what an agent made of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.91,0:00:19.22,Low,,0,0,0,,Opening it, a rib under each hinge knuckle swings into the rear wall: the lid jams around 40°, never reaching 110°.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.37,0:00:26.30,Low,,0,0,0,,The agent gets CAD tools over MCP, every requirement with its threshold, and the scoring rule. Never the fix.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.95,0:00:52.33,Low,,0,0,0,,Opus 5.5 on the judge set: 9 trials, mean 0.963. All gates passed, and every replay reproduces the graded parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.48,0:00:56.33,Low,,0,0,0,,Three trials stayed below the reference, all because of minimal change. Let's open the interesting ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.98,0:01:01.61,High,,0,0,0,,Opus 5.5 on L3: three different ribs, the whole assembly rotated in space. This is the replay of every tool call.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.76,0:01:06.08,High,,0,0,0,,It measures the interference at several angles and cuts sections through the ribs.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.23,0:01:12.04,High,,0,0,0,,Then one notch per rib, cut along the path the rib sweeps.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.19,0:01:17.98,High,,0,0,0,,The first fix passes every check: 23.3 mm³ removed. This is where Sonnet submitted, every time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.13,0:01:21.65,High,,0,0,0,,Opus instead undoes all three cuts...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.80,0:01:25.95,High,,0,0,0,,...and re-cuts each rib to its own swept radius: 3.70, 3.50 and 3.57 mm.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.10,0:01:33.14,High,,0,0,0,,Then it re-checks every requirement one by one before submitting.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.29,0:01:37.13,High,,0,0,0,,Submitted at 14.8 mm³, 0.93× the best known fix. Reward 1.0.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.78,0:01:44.61,Low,,0,0,0,,Same trial, from behind the wall. Red = material removed. Left: the reference fix. Right: Opus.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.76,0:01:52.00,Low,,0,0,0,,Both size each notch to its own rib: the reference volume is 15.9 mm³, Opus removed 14.8 mm³ (0.93×).
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.65,0:01:59.46,Low,,0,0,0,,Another Opus attempt at the same task. The reference cuts differ per rib; Opus copied one notch three times.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.61,0:02:04.66,Low,,0,0,0,,24.7 mm³ = 1.55× the best known fix, submitted after its first passing check. Reward 0.714.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.81,0:02:11.87,Low,,0,0,0,,Its explanation: “I didn't try to shrink the notches further because the clearance and seal margins are already small.”
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.52,0:02:19.76,Low,,0,0,0,,Sonnet 5.5 on the same task: identical rectangular pockets instead of a relief that follows the rib's sweep.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.91,0:02:24.96,Low,,0,0,0,,37.6 mm³ = 2.37× the necessary material, past the zero line for minimal change. Reward 0.400.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.11,0:02:31.43,Low,,0,0,0,,And it knew: “I did not try to shrink the pockets further, so some of the minimal-change score may be left on the table.”
